<p>Corpus Christi water damage claims come from many sources: a supply line that bursts behind the refrigerator, a water heater that fails in the garage, a slab leak, an overflowing washing machine, or rain blowing through a roof that a storm just opened up. Water spreads fast, wicks into drywall and cabinets, and can lead to mold within days in Coastal Bend humidity. If you own a home or business in Corpus Christi, Nueces County, or nearby communities, this page explains how water damage claims generally work, why they are often disputed, and how a public adjuster may help.</p>

<h2>Common Causes of Corpus Christi Water Damage Claims</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Plumbing failures</strong> &ndash; burst or cracked pipes, failed fittings, and broken supply lines to sinks, toilets, and ice makers.</li>
<li><strong>Appliance leaks</strong> &ndash; water heaters, washing machines, dishwashers, and refrigerators.</li>
<li><strong>Slab leaks</strong> &ndash; leaks in pipes under slab-on-grade homes, which are common in the area.</li>
<li><strong>HVAC problems</strong> &ndash; clogged condensate lines and overflowing drain pans, often in attics.</li>
<li><strong>Freeze damage</strong> &ndash; pipes that split during hard freezes.</li>
<li><strong>Storm-created openings</strong> &ndash; rain entering through roof, window, or wall damage caused by wind or hail. See <a href="/services/roof-damage-insurance-claims/">roof damage insurance claims</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Freezes are rare on the Coastal Bend, but they do happen, and many homes are not built for them. During the February 2021 winter storm, Corpus Christi International Airport recorded a low of 17&deg;F on February 15, a daily record, and stayed below freezing all day. Many homeowners found split pipes once temperatures rose. Our article on <a href="/freeze-damage-burst-pipe-claims-corpus-christi/">freeze damage and burst pipe claims</a> covers that kind of loss in detail.</p>

<h2>What Water Damage Policies Usually Cover and Exclude</h2>
<p>Coverage depends heavily on where the water came from and how long it was leaking. The table below shows general patterns; your policy wording controls.</p>
